---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Fourfold from "../../components/Fourfold.astro";
---
<Base
  order="local-pastors"
  title="The Fellowship of Local Pastors and Associate Members"
  description="Licensed pastors share with the elders the responsibilities and duties of a pastor for this fourfold ministry, within the context of their appointment. An independent project of local pastors and associate members, made visible one conference at a time."
  image="https://fellowshipoflocalpastors.org/og-landing.png"
  url="https://fellowshipoflocalpastors.org/"
>
  <header class="hero">
    <div class="frame" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="hero-text">
      <p class="label">The United Methodist Church</p>
      <h1>The Fellowship of Local Pastors and Associate Members</h1>
      <blockquote>
        "Each annual conference shall organize a Fellowship of Local Pastors and Associate Members&hellip; The Fellowship will provide mutual support for its members for the sake of the life and mission of the church."
        <cite>The Book of Discipline, &para; 323</cite>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section class="conferences">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="label">Conference chapters</p>
        <h2>Find your fellowship</h2>
        <div class="confgrid">
          <article class="confcard">
            <h3>R&iacute;o Texas Conference</h3>
            <p>A public prayer wall and the calendar of retreats and gatherings for the local pastors and associate members of the R&iacute;o Texas Annual Conference.</p>
            <a class="go" href="https://riotexas.fellowshipoflocalpastors.org">riotexas.fellowshipoflocalpastors.org &rarr;</a>
          </article>
          <article class="confcard invite">
            <h3>Your conference</h3>
            <p>This site is built to grow. If your conference's Fellowship of Local Pastors and Associate Members would like a home here &mdash; prayer, calendar, and more &mdash; we would be glad to help you start one.</p>
            <a class="go" href="mailto:hello@fellowshipoflocalpastors.org">Write to us &rarr;</a>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <Fourfold
      framed
      intro="Licensed pastors share with the elders the responsibilities and duties of a pastor for this fourfold ministry, within the context of their appointment."
      items={[
        { name: "Word", sub: "preaching · teaching · counsel", body: "To preach the Word of God, lead in worship, teach the Scriptures, and engage the people in study and witness — ensuring the faithful transmission of the Christian faith." },
        { name: "Sacrament", sub: "font · table", body: "To administer the sacraments of baptism and the Supper of the Lord according to Christ's ordinance, and to encourage the congregational use of the means of grace." },
        { name: "Order", sub: "administration · oversight · connection", body: "To order the life of the church for mission and ministry; to equip lay leadership; to administer the provisions of the Discipline within the connection." },
        { name: "Service", sub: "servant ministry · servant leadership", body: "To embody the teachings of Jesus in servant ministries, building the body of Christ as a caring and giving community, extending the ministry of Christ to the world." },
      ]}
    />

    <section class="purpose">
      <div class="wrap cols">
        <h2>Mutual support, for the sake of the mission</h2>
        <div>
          <p>Every local pastor and associate member belongs to the Fellowship &mdash; gathered for continuing formation, a bond of unity and common commitment, and relationships of mutual support and trust (&para; 323). But between annual conferences, that fellowship can be hard to see.</p>
          <p>This site exists to make the ordinary life of the Fellowship visible: the prayers we carry and the days we set apart to gather. It begins with what can be shared publicly, and it grows as the Fellowship asks it to.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Fragment slot="footer">
    <span class="mark">The Fellowship of Local Pastors and Associate Members</span>
    <p>An independent project of local pastors and associate members, for local pastors and associate members. Not an official agency of The United Methodist Church. Quotations from <em>The Book of Discipline of The United Methodist Church</em> are used for the Fellowship's formation and reference.</p>
    <p class="siblings">The other orders: <a href="https://orderofelders.org">The Order of Elders</a> &middot; <a href="https://orderofdeacons.org">The Order of Deacons</a></p>
  </Fragment>
</Base>

<style>
  /* ---------- hero: the appointment, a bounded frame ---------- */
  .hero { position: relative; text-align: center; padding: 96px 24px 84px; }
  .frame {
    position: absolute; inset: 28px; border: 2px solid var(--red); pointer-events: none;
  }
  .frame::after {
    content: "\271B"; position: absolute; left: 50%; bottom: -10px; transform: translateX(-50%);
    color: var(--gold); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1; background: var(--paper); padding: 0 8px;
  }
  .hero-text { position: relative; z-index: 1; }
  .hero .label { color: var(--smoke); }
  .hero h1 {
    font-family: "EB Garamond", serif; font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 6vw, 3.8rem);
    letter-spacing: .01em; line-height: 1.1;
    margin: .5rem 0 1.6rem;
  }
  .hero blockquote {
    max-width: 560px; margin: 0 auto;
    font-family: "EB Garamond", serif; font-style: italic;
    font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 2.4vw, 1.4rem); line-height: 1.5; color: var(--red-deep);
  }
  .hero cite {
    display: block; margin-top: 1rem; font-style: normal;
    font-family: "Archivo", sans-serif; font-size: .72rem; font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: .18em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--smoke);
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .frame { inset: 16px; }
    .hero { padding-top: 72px; }
  }

  /* ---------- conferences ---------- */
  .conferences { border-top: 1px solid var(--hair); padding: 84px 0; }
  .conferences .label { color: var(--red); }
  .conferences h2 { font-family: "EB Garamond", serif; font-weight: 500; font-size: 2.2rem; margin: .4rem 0 2rem; }
  .confgrid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 28px; }
  @media (max-width: 680px) { .confgrid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .confcard {
    border: 1px solid var(--hair); background: #FBFAF5; padding: 36px 34px;
    border-top: 4px solid var(--red);
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: .6rem;
  }
  .confcard.invite { border-top-color: var(--gold); background: transparent; }
  .confcard h3 { font-family: "EB Garamond", serif; font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.5rem; }
  .confcard p { font-size: .97rem; color: #3B362E; flex: 1; }
  .confcard .go { font-family: "Archivo", sans-serif; font-weight: 600; font-size: .78rem; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; }

  /* ---------- purpose ---------- */
  .purpose { border-top: 1px solid var(--hair); padding: 84px 0; }
  .purpose .cols { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 280px 1fr; gap: 48px; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .purpose .cols { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 20px; } }
  .purpose h2 { font-family: "EB Garamond", serif; font-weight: 500; font-size: 2rem; line-height: 1.2; }
  .purpose p { margin-bottom: 1rem; max-width: 58ch; }
</style>
